{%- comment -%}
  The blog article (direction D of docs/blog/02-PROPOSAL.md, Victor 26 Oct): a centred header with the
  homepage eyebrow, the title, the standfirst and a rule with date, reading time and Share; the
  featured picture wide; the legal pages' contents menu beside a 680px text column; the study links
  of the body as a Sources card; Keep reading with thumbnails. The homepage end CTA is its own section
  after this one (templates/article.json). Styles: assets/kc-blog.css. Menu: assets/kc-blog-contents.js.

  The blocks keep their job in the theme editor: featured_image shows or hides the picture, title the
  date, share the Share button, content the body; their order no longer moves the parts, because the
  layout is fixed. App blocks print after the body.
{%- endcomment -%}
{{ 'kc-blog.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'section-blog-post.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<script src="{{ 'kc-blog-contents.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

{%- liquid
  assign kc_image_block = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'featured_image' | first
  assign kc_title_block = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'title' | first
  assign kc_share_block = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'share' | first
  assign kc_content_block = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'content' | first

  # Reading time: words at 200 a minute, rounded up. Every tag end gets a space first, so words in
  # two paragraphs are never counted as one.
  assign kc_words = article.content | replace: '>', '> ' | strip_html | split: ' ' | size
  assign kc_minutes = kc_words | divided_by: 200.0 | ceil | at_least: 1

  assign kc_body = article.content
-%}

{%- capture kc_body -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Headings (R90 B3). The title is the page's only h1 and the body's headings never skip a level, so
    the outline is h1 title, h2 sections, h3 and h4 below them. A body that uses h1 for its sections
    (the nano article) moves down one level. Then each heading is at most one level below the one
    before it (the title counts as h1), and at most h4: the wellness article's opening h5 becomes h2,
    the nano article's h3 under an h1 becomes h3. Wording and order are untouched; only the tag
    changes. '<h' also starts <hr> and <header>; those parts do not start with a digit and pass through.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign kc_shift = 0
    if kc_body contains '<h1'
      assign kc_shift = 1
    endif
    assign kc_prev = 1
    assign kc_h_parts = kc_body | split: '<h'
  -%}
  {%- for kc_part in kc_h_parts -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign kc_first = kc_part | slice: 0
      assign kc_is_heading = false
      unless forloop.first
        case kc_first
          when '1', '2', '3', '4', '5', '6'
            assign kc_is_heading = true
        endcase
      endunless
    -%}
    {%- unless kc_is_heading -%}
      {%- unless forloop.first -%}<h{%- endunless -%}{{- kc_part -}}
      {%- continue -%}
    {%- endunless -%}
    {%- liquid
      # A heading with no text (the wellness article opens with an h5 holding only &nbsp;) prints as a
      # paragraph: a screen reader would announce an empty heading, and it takes no part in the levels
      assign kc_old_close = '</h' | append: kc_first | append: '>'
      assign kc_heading_text = kc_part | split: kc_old_close | first | split: '>' | slice: 1, 999 | join: '>' | strip_html | replace: '&nbsp;', '' | strip
    -%}
    {%- if kc_heading_text == blank -%}
      <p{{- kc_part | slice: 1, kc_part.size | replace_first: kc_old_close, '</p>' -}}
      {%- continue -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign kc_old = kc_first | plus: 0
      assign kc_level = kc_old | plus: kc_shift
      assign kc_max = kc_prev | plus: 1
      if kc_level > kc_max
        assign kc_level = kc_max
      endif
      if kc_level > 4
        assign kc_level = 4
      endif
      if kc_level < 2
        assign kc_level = 2
      endif
      assign kc_prev = kc_level
      assign kc_close_old = '</h' | append: kc_old | append: '>'
      assign kc_close_new = '</h' | append: kc_level | append: '>'
      assign kc_rest = kc_part | slice: 1, kc_part.size | replace_first: kc_close_old, kc_close_new
    -%}
    <h{{- kc_level -}}{{- kc_rest -}}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- capture kc_body_html -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Body pictures. Every picture keeps its tag exactly as the article wrote it; only lazy loading and
    async decoding are added when the tag has none. Hotfix 26 Oct: on the store, looking a picture up
    in Files by name and passing it to image_url printed "Liquid error: invalid url input" in place of
    every body picture, a failure the local liquidjs render could not show. Reserving each picture's
    size (R90 B2) comes back only once a way is checked on a real Shopify render.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign kc_img_parts = kc_body | split: '<img ' -%}
  {%- for kc_part in kc_img_parts -%}
    {%- if forloop.first -%}{{ kc_part }}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- assign kc_tag = kc_part | split: '>' | first -%}
    {%- assign kc_after = kc_part | remove_first: kc_tag | remove_first: '>' -%}
    <img{% unless kc_tag contains 'loading=' %} loading="lazy"{% endunless %}{% unless kc_tag contains 'decoding=' %} decoding="async"{% endunless %} {{ kc_tag }}>
    {{- kc_after -}}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- capture kc_sources -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Sources: the links in the body that point to a study publisher, in the order they appear, each once.
    The link text is the article's own anchor text; the publisher name comes from the link's host.
    Consumer sites (Healthline, Forbes, WebMD …) are not on the list and stay inline only.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign kc_hosts = 'pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov|PubMed Central,ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc|PubMed Central,pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov|PubMed,sciencedirect.com|ScienceDirect,mdpi.com|MDPI,researchgate.net|ResearchGate,diabetesjournals.org|Diabetes Care,jech.bmj.com|Journal of Epidemiology & Community Health,biomedcentral.com|BMC Public Health,healthopenresearch.org|Health Open Research,jebms.org|JEBMS,hindawi.com|Hindawi,intechopen.com|IntechOpen,biointerfaceresearch.com|Biointerface Research,doi.org|DOI' | split: ',' -%}
  {%- assign kc_seen = '|' -%}
  {%- assign kc_parts = article.content | split: '<a ' -%}
  {%- for kc_part in kc_parts offset: 1 -%}
    {%- unless kc_part contains 'href="' -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endunless -%}
    {%- assign kc_tag = kc_part | split: '>' | first -%}
    {%- assign kc_href = kc_tag | split: 'href="' | last | split: '"' | first -%}
    {%- assign kc_label = '' -%}
    {%- for kc_pair in kc_hosts -%}
      {%- assign kc_host = kc_pair | split: '|' | first -%}
      {%- if kc_href contains kc_host -%}
        {%- assign kc_label = kc_pair | split: '|' | last -%}
        {%- break -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
    {%- if kc_label == blank -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- assign kc_key = kc_href | split: '#' | first | append: '|' -%}
    {%- if kc_seen contains kc_key -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- assign kc_seen = kc_seen | append: kc_key -%}
    {%- assign kc_text = kc_part | split: '</a>' | first | remove_first: kc_tag | remove_first: '>' | strip_html | strip -%}
    {%- if kc_text.size < 4 -%}{%- assign kc_text = kc_label | escape -%}{%- endif -%}
    <li class="kc-blog-sources__item">
      <a class="kc-blog-sources__link" href="{{ kc_href }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <span class="kc-blog-sources__title">{{ kc_text }}</span>
        <span class="kc-blog-sources__host">{{ kc_label | escape }}</span>
        <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none"><path d="M14 6V2H10M14 2L6.66667 9.33334M12 8.66667V12.6667C12 13.0203 11.8595 13.3594 11.6095 13.6095C11.3594 13.8595 11.0203 14 10.6667 14H3.33333C2.97971 14 2.64057 13.8595 2.39052 13.6095C2.14048 13.3594 2 13.0203 2 12.6667V5.33333C2 4.97971 2.14048 4.64057 2.39052 4.39053C2.64057 4.14048 2.97971 4 3.33333 4H7.33333" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'accessibility.link_messages.new_window' | t }}</span>
      </a>
    </li>
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

<article class="kc-blog">
  <header class="kc-blog__head">
    <div class="kc-blog__wrap">
      <a class="kc-blog__eyebrow kc-caption-subheading subtitle-item" href="{{ blog.url }}">{{ blog.title | escape }}</a>
      <h1 class="kc-blog__title"{% if kc_title_block %} {{ kc_title_block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}>{{ article.title | escape }}</h1>
      {%- if article.excerpt != blank -%}
        <p class="kc-blog__standfirst">{{ article.excerpt | strip_html | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      <div class="kc-blog__bar">
        <ul class="kc-blog__meta" role="list">
          {%- if kc_title_block == blank or kc_title_block.settings.blog_show_date -%}
            <li>{{ article.published_at | time_tag: format: 'date' }}</li>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if kc_title_block.settings.blog_show_author -%}
            <li>{{ article.author | escape }}</li>
          {%- endif -%}
          <li>{{ 'blogs.article.reading_time' | t: minutes: kc_minutes }}</li>
        </ul>
        {%- if kc_share_block -%}
          {%- assign kc_share_url = request.origin | append: article.url -%}
          <div class="kc-blog__share-wrap">
            {%- render 'share-button', block: kc_share_block, share_link: kc_share_url -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  {%- if kc_image_block and article.image -%}
    <figure class="kc-blog__figure" {{ kc_image_block.shopify_attributes }}>
      <div class="kc-blog__media" style="--kc-media-natural-width: {{ article.image.width | divided_by: 10.0 }}rem;">
        {{-
          article.image
          | image_url: width: 2560
          | image_tag:
            widths: '550, 750, 1100, 1500, 1920, 2560',
            sizes: '(min-width: 1344px) 1280px, (min-width: 641px) calc(100vw - 64px), 100vw',
            loading: 'eager',
            fetchpriority: 'high'
        -}}
      </div>
    </figure>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="kc-blog__main">
    <div class="kc-blog__layout">
      <aside class="kc-blog__toc" data-kc-blog-contents-box>
        <p class="kc-blog-toc__eyebrow subtitle-item opacity-xl" aria-hidden="true">{{ 'blogs.article.on_this_page' | t }}</p>
        <nav aria-label="{{ 'blogs.article.on_this_page' | t | escape }}">
          <ul class="kc-blog-toc__list" role="list" data-kc-blog-contents></ul>
        </nav>
      </aside>

      <div class="kc-blog__text">
        <div class="kc-blog__body rte"{% if kc_content_block %} {{ kc_content_block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}>
          {{- kc_body_html -}}
        </div>

        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {%- if block.type == '@app' -%}
            {% render block %}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}

        {%- if kc_sources != blank -%}
          <div class="kc-blog__end">
            <aside class="kc-blog-sources" aria-labelledby="KcBlogSources-{{ section.id }}">
              <h2 class="kc-blog-sources__heading" id="KcBlogSources-{{ section.id }}" data-kc-blog-toc-extra>
                {{- 'blogs.article.sources' | t -}}
              </h2>
              <ul class="kc-blog-sources__list" role="list">
                {{- kc_sources -}}
              </ul>
            </aside>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- liquid
    assign kc_related_count = 0
    capture kc_related
      for kc_other in blog.articles
        if kc_other.id == article.id
          continue
        endif
        render 'kc-blog-row', article: kc_other, heading: 'h3', show_excerpt: false
        assign kc_related_count = kc_related_count | plus: 1
        if kc_related_count == 3
          break
        endif
      endfor
    endcapture
  -%}
  {%- if kc_related_count > 0 -%}
    <div class="kc-blog-related">
      <div class="kc-blog__layout">
        <div class="kc-blog__text">
          <h2 class="kc-blog__section-heading">{{ 'blogs.article.keep_reading' | t }}</h2>
          <ul class="kc-blog-list" role="list">
            {{- kc_related -}}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if blog.comments_enabled? -%}
    <div class="article-template__comment-wrapper background-secondary">
      <div
        id="comments"
        class="page-width page-width--narrow{% if settings.animations_reveal_on_scroll %} scroll-trigger animate--slide-in{% endif %}"
      >
        {%- if article.comments_count > 0 -%}
          {%- assign anchorId = '#Comments-' | append: article.id -%}

          <h2 id="Comments-{{ article.id }}" tabindex="-1">
            {{ 'blogs.article.comments' | t: count: article.comments_count }}
          </h2>
          {% paginate article.comments by 5 %}
            <div class="article-template__comments">
              {%- if comment.status == 'pending' and comment.content -%}
                <article id="{{ comment.id }}" class="article-template__comments-comment">
                  {{ comment.content }}
                  <footer class="right">
                    <span class="circle-divider caption-with-letter-spacing">{{ comment.author }}</span>
                  </footer>
                </article>
              {%- endif -%}

              {%- for comment in article.comments -%}
                <article id="{{ comment.id }}" class="article-template__comments-comment">
                  {{ comment.content }}
                  <footer class="right">
                    <span class="circle-divider caption-with-letter-spacing">{{ comment.author }}</span
                    ><span class="caption-with-letter-spacing">
                      {{- comment.created_at | time_tag: format: 'date' -}}
                    </span>
                  </footer>
                </article>
              {%- endfor -%}
              {% render 'pagination', paginate: paginate, anchor: anchorId %}
            </div>
          {% endpaginate %}
        {%- endif -%}
        {% form 'new_comment', article %}
          {%- liquid
            assign post_message = 'blogs.article.success'
            if blog.moderated? and comment.status == 'unapproved'
              assign post_message = 'blogs.article.success_moderated'
            endif
          -%}
          <h2>{{ 'blogs.article.comment_form_title' | t }}</h2>
          {%- if form.errors -%}
            <div class="form__message" role="alert">
              <h3 class="form-status caption-large text-body" tabindex="-1" autofocus>
                <span class="svg-wrapper">
                  {{- 'icon-error.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
                </span>
                {{ 'templates.contact.form.error_heading' | t }}
              </h3>
            </div>
            <ul class="form-status-list caption-large">
              {%- for field in form.errors -%}
                <li>
                  <a href="#CommentForm-{{ field }}" class="link">
                    {%- if form.errors.translated_fields[field] contains 'author' -%}
                      {{ 'blogs.article.name' | t }}
                    {%- elsif form.errors.translated_fields[field] contains 'body' -%}
                      {{ 'blogs.article.message' | t }}
                    {%- else -%}
                      {{ form.errors.translated_fields[field] }}
                    {%- endif -%}
                    {{ form.errors.messages[field] }}
                  </a>
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          {%- elsif form.posted_successfully? -%}
            <div class="form-status-list form__message" role="status">
              <h3 class="form-status" tabindex="-1" autofocus>
                <span class="svg-wrapper">
                  {{- 'icon-success.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
                </span>
                {{ post_message | t }}
              </h3>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}

          <div
            {% if blog.moderated? == false %}
              class="article-template__comments-fields"
            {% endif %}
          >
            <div class="article-template__comment-fields">
              <div class="field field--with-error">
                <input
                  type="text"
                  name="comment[author]"
                  id="CommentForm-author"
                  class="field__input"
                  autocomplete="name"
                  value="{{ form.author }}"
                  aria-required="true"
                  required
                  {% if form.errors contains 'author' %}
                    aria-invalid="true"
                    aria-describedby="CommentForm-author-error"
                  {% endif %}
                  placeholder="{{ 'blogs.article.name' | t }}"
                >
                <label class="field__label" for="CommentForm-author">
                  {{- 'blogs.article.name' | t }}
                  <span aria-hidden="true">*</span></label
                >
                {%- if form.errors contains 'author' -%}
                  <small id="CommentForm-author-error">
                    <span class="form__message">
                      <span class="svg-wrapper">
                        {{- 'icon-error.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
                      </span>
                      {{- 'blogs.article.name' | t }}
                      {{ form.errors.messages.author }}.</span
                    >
                  </small>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
              <div class="field field--with-error">
                <input
                  type="email"
                  name="comment[email]"
                  id="CommentForm-email"
                  autocomplete="email"
                  class="field__input"
                  value="{{ form.email }}"
                  autocorrect="off"
                  autocapitalize="off"
                  aria-required="true"
                  required
                  {% if form.errors contains 'email' %}
                    aria-invalid="true"
                    aria-describedby="CommentForm-email-error"
                  {% endif %}
                  placeholder="{{ 'blogs.article.email' | t }}"
                >
                <label class="field__label" for="CommentForm-email">
                  {{- 'blogs.article.email' | t }}
                  <span aria-hidden="true">*</span></label
                >
                {%- if form.errors contains 'email' -%}
                  <small id="CommentForm-email-error">
                    <span class="form__message">
                      <span class="svg-wrapper">
                        {{- 'icon-error.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
                      </span>
                      {{- 'blogs.article.email' | t }}
                      {{ form.errors.messages.email }}.</span
                    >
                  </small>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="field field--with-error">
              <textarea
                rows="5"
                name="comment[body]"
                id="CommentForm-body"
                class="text-area field__input"
                aria-required="true"
                required
                {% if form.errors contains 'body' %}
                  aria-invalid="true"
                  aria-describedby="CommentForm-body-error"
                {% endif %}
                placeholder="{{ 'blogs.article.message' | t }}"
              >{{ form.body }}</textarea>
              <label class="form__label field__label" for="CommentForm-body">
                {{- 'blogs.article.message' | t }}
                <span aria-hidden="true">*</span></label
              >
            </div>
            {%- if form.errors contains 'body' -%}
              <small id="CommentForm-body-error">
                <span class="form__message">
                  <span class="svg-wrapper">
                    {{- 'icon-error.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
                  </span>
                  {{- 'blogs.article.message' | t }}
                  {{ form.errors.messages.body }}.</span
                >
              </small>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
          {%- if blog.moderated? -%}
            <p class="article-template__comment-warning caption">{{ 'blogs.article.moderated' | t }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          <input type="submit" class="button" value="{{ 'blogs.article.post' | t }}">
        {% endform %}
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</article>

<script type="application/ld+json">
  {{ article | structured_data }}
</script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:sections.main-article.name",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "@app"
    },
    {
      "type": "featured_image",
      "name": "t:sections.main-article.blocks.featured_image.name",
      "limit": 1,
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "image_height",
          "options": [
            {
              "value": "adapt",
              "label": "t:sections.main-article.blocks.featured_image.settings.image_height.options__1.label"
            },
            {
              "value": "small",
              "label": "t:sections.main-article.blocks.featured_image.settings.image_height.options__2.label"
            },
            {
              "value": "medium",
              "label": "t:sections.main-article.blocks.featured_image.settings.image_height.options__3.label"
            },
            {
              "value": "large",
              "label": "t:sections.main-article.blocks.featured_image.settings.image_height.options__4.label"
            }
          ],
          "default": "adapt",
          "label": "t:sections.main-article.blocks.featured_image.settings.image_height.label"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "title",
      "name": "t:sections.main-article.blocks.title.name",
      "limit": 1,
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "checkbox",
          "id": "blog_show_date",
          "default": true,
          "label": "t:sections.main-article.blocks.title.settings.blog_show_date.label"
        },
        {
          "type": "checkbox",
          "id": "blog_show_author",
          "default": false,
          "label": "t:sections.main-article.blocks.title.settings.blog_show_author.label"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "content",
      "name": "t:sections.main-article.blocks.content.name",
      "limit": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "share",
      "name": "t:sections.main-article.blocks.share.name",
      "limit": 2,
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "share_label",
          "label": "t:sections.main-article.blocks.share.settings.text.label",
          "default": "t:sections.main-article.blocks.share.settings.text.default"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
